{% section #step-2 step=2 title="Add the MCP server" %}

Connect the Appwrite MCP server to Claude Desktop for deeper integration with the Appwrite API and documentation.

Use a custom connector to connect Claude Desktop directly to the hosted Appwrite MCP server. This setup does not require Node.js or a local configuration file.

1. Open **Customize > Connectors** in Claude Desktop.
2. Choose **Add custom connector** and name it **Appwrite**.
3. Enter the remote MCP server URL:

```text
https://mcp.appwrite.io/
```

4. Follow the connector setup, then click **Connect** to sign in to your Appwrite account and authorize access when prompted.

For Team and Enterprise organizations, someone with permission to manage connectors must add it before members can connect. See [Claude's custom connector guide](https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11175166-get-started-with-custom-connectors-using-remote-mcp) for current availability and setup options.

{% info title="Self-hosted Appwrite" %}

The hosted connector authenticates against Appwrite Cloud. For a self-hosted instance, follow the [local MCP server setup](/docs/tooling/ai/mcp-servers#self-hosted) instead.

{% /info %}

{% /section %}

{% section #step-3 step=3 title="Verify MCP tools" %}

In a conversation, open **Connectors** from the **+** menu and enable **Appwrite**. Confirm that the connector is connected and its tools are available.

{% /section %}

{% section #step-4 step=4 title="Test the integration" %}

Try out the following example prompts:

**Example prompts:**

- `Create a new user in my Appwrite project`
- `List all databases in my project`
- `Show me the tables in my database`
- `How do I set up real-time subscriptions in Appwrite?`
- `Show me how to authenticate users with OAuth`
- `How do I implement file uploads with Appwrite Storage?`

![List users in Appwrite project](/images/docs/mcp/claude-desktop/claude-list-users.avif)

{% /section %}

{% section #local-bridge title="Alternative: local stdio bridge" %}

If custom connectors are unavailable in your environment, you can connect through a local stdio bridge instead. This alternative requires [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/en/download) and npm.

Open **Settings > Developer > Local MCP servers**, choose **Edit Config**, and add this entry to `claude_desktop_config.json`:

```json
{
    "mcpServers": {
        "appwrite": {
            "command": "npx",
            "args": [
                "-y",
                "mcp-remote@0.16.0",
                "https://mcp.appwrite.io/"
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

Restart Claude Desktop, then complete the Appwrite sign-in in your browser. The server appears under **Local MCP servers**.

If you see an `npx ENOENT` error, add `npx` to your `PATH` or use its full path in the configuration.

{% /section %}
